[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237335255","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3237335255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3237335255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9dDX","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T14:56:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T14:57:10Z","body":"Can you test with [beta6](https://godotengine.org/article/dev-snapshot-godot-4-5-beta-6/) just to make sure it's not already been fixed?\n\nAlso does this happen in 4.4.1?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237335255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237471773","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3237471773","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3237471773,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A9-Yd","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T15:40:45Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T15:40:45Z","body":"Just tested, it happends in beta7 and in 4.4.1.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237471773/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243191649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3243191649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3243191649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BTy1h","user":{"login":"voidiii","id":41127515,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTI3NTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41127515?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii","html_url":"https://github.com/voidiii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-01T20:09:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-01T20:09:03Z","body":"There is a simple fix: Use\n```\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t# Initial velocity (world −Z). Use local forward instead if you prefer (see below).\n\tlinear_velocity = Vector3(0.0, 0.0, -15.0)\n\tsleeping = false  # make sure it's awake so velocit\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n\t# Use the *current simulated* velocity (includes gravity & collisions)\n\tvar motion := linear_velocity * delta\n\tvar hit := move_and_collide(motion)\n\tif hit and not first_contact:\n\t\tprint(\"collision info!\", hit.get_collider(), hit.get_normal(), hit.get_position())\n\t\tfirst_contact = true\n```\ninstead of \n```\nvar hit := move_and_collide(Vector3(0.0, 0.0, -15.0) * delta)\n```\nThis way, both Godot Physics and Jolt Physics will behave the same and will give you the hit. Also it will fix the weird buggy motion in your wall scene. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243191649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243193136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3243193136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3243193136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BTzMw","user":{"login":"voidiii","id":41127515,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTI3NTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41127515?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii","html_url":"https://github.com/voidiii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-01T20:10:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-01T20:10:19Z","body":"I think this should be mentioned in the document that move_and_collide()'s first parameter should be the actual motion of the object itself (which is always changing due to gravity and stuff) instead of a constant fixed vector","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243193136/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246239550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3246239550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3246239550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bfa8-","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T17:39:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T17:39:43Z","body":"What I did as a workaround is to check the checkbox ‘Custom Integrator’ and add the gravity in the vector I pass to ‘move_and_collide()’. What you suggest makes sense too.\n\nHowever, I still think that Jolt and Godot Physics should be consistent, and it would make sense that Jolt’s move_and_collide() returns a collision when there is a collision.\n\nAlso, if we always need to pass linear_velocity to move_and_collide() as an argument, wouldn’t it be simpler not to have to pass it at all?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246239550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246790074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110091#issuecomment-3246790074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110091","id":3246790074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BhhW6","user":{"login":"voidiii","id":41127515,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTI3NTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41127515?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii","html_url":"https://github.com/voidiii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidiii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T21:06:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T21:06:55Z","body":"Yeah I thought it was weird too. I think move_and_collide() is for KinematicBody and CharacterBody instead of RigidBody. I know RigidBody inherits move_and_collide() from PhysicsBody so naturally it should also be able to use move_and_collide() but, given the parameter of this function, it looks like Godot wants whatever object that is calling this function to handle the velocity by itself, just like a CharacterBody. With RigidBody, Godot will handle velocity and everything, which makes passing velocity look weird. \n\nI am new to Godot though, so I can easily be wrong. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246790074/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]